= What Is It Like to Be a Bat? / 成为一只蝙蝠是什么感觉？

#html.p(id: "en-G001")[#text("Imagine knowing a bat's anatomy and the mechanisms of echolocation. Nagel asks whether this objective knowledge gives access to the experience of being that animal.")]

#zh(id: "G001")[#text("想象我们知道蝙蝠的解剖结构，也明白回声定位的机制。内格尔追问：这些客观知识，是否让我们能够进入作为这种动物的体验？")]

#html.p(id: "en-G002")[#text("The problem concerns the point of view carried by conscious experience. Imagining yourself flying in darkness may reveal your imagination without revealing the bat's experience.")]

#zh(id: "G002")[#text("问题涉及意识体验所带有的视角。想象自己在黑暗中飞行，可能揭示的是你的想象方式，而不是蝙蝠的体验。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G003")[#text("Read this beside Turing: a criterion for observable performance and an account of subjective experience address different questions. Their difference makes the pairing productive.")]

#zh(id: "G003")[#text("可以把它与图灵对照阅读：可观察行为的判定标准，与主观体验的解释，回答的是不同问题。正因为问题不同，两篇放在一起才有启发。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G004")[#text("Reading question: what would count as understanding an experience, and whose perspective would that understanding preserve? The article helps formulate the difficulty before offering an easy solution.")]

#zh(id: "G004")[#text("阅读时可以追问：什么才算理解一种体验？这种理解又保留了谁的视角？文章的价值在于先把困难说清楚，而不是急着给出轻松的答案。")]
